        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Kibbeh depends on "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "binding-meat"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "binding the meat"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " and couscous together into a smooth paste before shaping. This takes 3 to 4 minutes of firm kneading. The "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "baharat"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "baharat"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " spice blend is approximated here with cinnamon, allspice, and cumin, which together give the characteristic warm, aromatic quality."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Tip: chilling the shaped kibbeh for 20 minutes before frying helps them keep their shape in the pan."
          }
        ]
      },
